[E0348] Error: `?` on `Result<i64, i64>` needs the function to return one too
   ╭─[ err/101_propagation/main.wip:8:19 ]
   │
 8 │ fn plain(): i64 = ok()?                          // returns neither
   │                   ──┬──
   │                     ╰──── this function returns `i64`
   │
   │ Help: convert it first, with `mapErr`
   │
   │ Note: `?` returns the error as it is, unless the function's error type says how it is made from this one
───╯
[E0348] Error: `?` on `Result<i64, i64>` needs the function to return one too
   ╭─[ err/101_propagation/main.wip:9:42 ]
   │
 9 │ fn wrongError(): Result<i64, bool> = .Ok(ok()?)  // another error type
   │                                          ──┬──
   │                                            ╰──── this function returns `Result<i64, bool>`
   │
   │ Help: write `extend bool: From<i64>`, and `?` will use it; or convert it here with `mapErr`
   │
   │ Note: `?` returns the error as it is, unless the function's error type says how it is made from this one
───╯
[E0348] Error: `?` on `Option<i64>` needs the function to return one too
    ╭─[ err/101_propagation/main.wip:10:45 ]
    │
 10 │ fn optionInResult(): Result<i64, i64> = .Ok(opt()?)
    │                                             ───┬──
    │                                                ╰──── this function returns `Result<i64, i64>`
    │
    │ Note: `?` on an `Option` returns `.None`, so the function must return an `Option`
────╯
[E0348] Error: `?` needs an `Option` or a `Result`, and this is `i64`
    ╭─[ err/101_propagation/main.wip:12:40 ]
    │
 12 │ fn notEither(): Result<i64, i64> = .Ok(3?)       // not either type
    │                                        ─┬
    │                                         ╰── not an `Option` or a `Result`
    │
    │ Note: `?` takes the value, or returns the other variant to the caller
────╯
